/-!
# Can a prover close a generalization the original proof could not?

Every line below is a weakening `#fh_home_refute` REFUTED — the declaration's own proof term
fails against the weaker hypothesis. That verdict never meant the statement was false, only
that this proof did not survive. Nothing in this project has ever asked the other question.

A PROVED line is a theorem the system proposed and a prover established, by an argument the
original declaration did not use.
-/

